{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnumerationBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnumerationBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnumeration","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Permutation","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.YoungDiagram"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.card_cells_ofRowLens","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.card_cells_ofRowLens","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationBridge.lean#L103-L106","doc":"`#cells (ofRowLens w hw) = ∑w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.card_cellsOfRowLens","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.card_cellsOfRowLens","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationBridge.lean#L81-L101","doc":"**The Young diagram of a row-length list has exactly `∑l` cells** (a Mathlib gap: there is no\n`card (cellsOfRowLens w) = w.sum` in the pinned toolchain).  Proved by induction on the recursive\n`cellsOfRowLens`: each cons adds a fresh row `{0} ×ˢ range a` (card `a`) disjoint from the rest\n(whose first coordinate is `Nat.succ _ ≥ 1`).  This is the cardinality `n` that the\n`StandardYoungTableau.bijOn` field ranges over (`Set.Icc 1 μ.cells.card`), pinning it to `∑l` — the\nload-bearing fact for the remaining `numSYTenum = dimSYT` bijection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.mem_standardFillings_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.mem_standardFillings_iff","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationBridge.lean#L74-L79","doc":"A list is a standard filling of shape `l` iff it is a permutation of `[1,…,∑l]` that passes\n`isStdFilling` — the clean characterisation the structural bijection will match against. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.numSYTenum_eq_length_standardFillings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.numSYTenum_eq_length_standardFillings","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationBridge.lean#L69-L72","doc":"`numSYTenum` is the length of the list of standard fillings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.standardFillings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.standardFillings","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationBridge.lean#L65-L67","doc":"The flat fillings of shape `l`: permutations of `[1,…,∑l]` that pass `isStdFilling`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.mem_allPerms_iff_perm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.mem_allPerms_iff_perm","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationBridge.lean#L61-L63","doc":"Membership in `allPerms l` is exactly being a permutation of `l`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.allPerms_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.allPerms_eq","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationBridge.lean#L51-L59","doc":"The hand-rolled `allPerms` is exactly Mathlib's `List.permutations'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.insertEverywhere_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.insertEverywhere_eq","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationBridge.lean#L43-L49","doc":"All ways to insert `x` into `l` are exactly Mathlib's `permutations'Aux` (definitionally, up to\nthe structural recursion). ","signatureChunk":0}]}